window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b225-4e3e07e7c9770cfa.json"]={sha256:"4e3e07e7c9770cfafbdd871646df8b4e484b07f387bc2a96cbf6a925cdbdb3f8",value:{"id":"b225","title":"新加坡濱海堤壩","titleEn":"Marina Barrage","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以新加坡濱海堤壩為入口，深入都市逕流、潮位排水、抽水能源與水庫水質。十個單元各自對應不同的荷載路徑、能量交換或監測問題，從守恆式建立量化估算，再檢查量測配置是否能辨認真正失效原因。工程史實只採用列明範圍的公開一手資料；所有模型輸入另標為教學假設，成果是可追溯的工程判讀紀錄。","summaryEn":"Using Marina Barrage as its entry point, this course examines urban runoff, tidal drainage, pumping energy and reservoir water quality. Ten units address different load paths, energy exchanges or monitoring questions, starting with conservation-based estimates and testing whether observations distinguish failure causes. Historical statements use scoped primary evidence. Numerical model inputs are separately identified as teaching assumptions, producing a traceable engineering interpretation record.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-systems","subcategoryTitle":"防潮、航運與大壩施工","subcategoryTitleEn":"Tidal barriers, navigation and dam construction","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-systems","learningTags":["water","water-systems","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-gate","architectureNodes":[["集水區逕流峰值","Catchment runoff peak"],["低潮重力排水","Low-tide gravity drainage"],["並聯泵與系統曲線","Parallel pumps and system curve"],["鹽水入侵質量平衡","Salt intrusion mass balance"],["複合事件與失效組合","Compound events and failure combinations"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-gate","labels":["集水區逕流峰值","低潮重力排水","並聯泵與系統曲線","鹽水入侵質量平衡","複合事件與失效組合"],"labelsEn":["Catchment runoff peak","Low-tide gravity drainage","Parallel pumps and system curve","Salt intrusion mass balance","Compound events and failure combinations"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課原創比較練習分兩個相互獨立的物理模型。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設集水區2 km²、C=0.75、雨強60 mm/h且歷時超過集流時間；Q=0.278CiA=25.02 m³/s，未含渠道滯蓄。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設淨入流80 m³/s持續30 min、有效水面3 km²，Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m；只作固定面積短時估算。先逐一圈出公式內的控制體、力方向或時間尺度，再把每項輸入的量綱換成一致單位。第二人只根據輸入重算結果，不抄第一人的中間數字。最後指出這兩個估算尚未包含的空間變化、非線性及量測誤差；若將結果用於另一座工程，必須重建其幾何、材料與邊界條件，不能挪用本練習的假設。 降雨敏感度固定集水區A=2 km²與逕流係數C=0.75，只將雨強i由60改為90 mm/h；兩情境都假設降雨歷時超過集流時間。沿用同一單位換算式Q=0.278CiA，流量由25.02增至37.53 m³/s，增加50%。此線性比較未納入C隨飽和改變或渠道滯蓄，也不是泵站所需容量的直接決定。","textEn":"This original comparison exercise uses two independent physical models. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume area 2 km², C=0.75 and intensity 60 mm/h lasting beyond concentration time. Q=0.278CiA=25.02 m³/s, excluding channel storage. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume net inflow 80 m³/s over thirty minutes and effective area 3 km². Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m, a short-duration constant-area estimate. First identify the control volume, force direction or time scale in each relation, then convert every input to consistent units. A second reviewer recalculates from the inputs without copying intermediate numbers. Finally identify spatial variability, nonlinear effects and measurement errors omitted by both estimates. Transfer to another structure requires rebuilding its geometry, material description and boundary conditions; the assumed classroom inputs are not transferable design or operating parameters. Hold catchment area A=2 km² and runoff coefficient C=0.75 fixed, changing only rainfall intensity i from 60 to 90 mm/h; both storms last beyond concentration time. With the same unit-converted relation Q=0.278CiA, flow increases from 25.02 to 37.53 m³/s, or 50%. This linear comparison excludes saturation-related changes in C and channel storage and does not directly determine pumping capacity.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b225-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「集水區逕流峰值」與「庫容與淨入流」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Catchment runoff peak\" and \"Storage and net inflow\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b225-v15-01","title":"集水區逕流峰值：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Catchment runoff peak: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「集水區逕流峰值」如何影響新加坡濱海堤壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Catchment runoff peak” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"都市不透水面提高快速逕流比例，但降雨空間與集流時間控制峰值。合理化公式適合指定的小型集水區條件，不能直接代表整個大型水庫入流歷線。 假設集水區2 km²、C=0.75、雨強60 mm/h且歷時超過集流時間；Q=0.278CiA=25.02 m³/s，未含渠道滯蓄。 短時局部暴雨可能不符合均勻降雨假設，排水瓶頸也會改變峰值時間。把每個分區峰值直接相加，可能錯估各峰不同時到達的真實入流。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「集水區逕流峰值」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Impervious surfaces increase rapid runoff, while rainfall distribution and concentration time control the peak. The rational method applies to specified small-catchment conditions, not a complete large-reservoir inflow hydrograph. Assume area 2 km², C=0.75 and intensity 60 mm/h lasting beyond concentration time. Q=0.278CiA=25.02 m³/s, excluding channel storage. Brief localized storms violate uniform rainfall assumptions, and drainage bottlenecks alter peak timing. Adding every subcatchment peak directly can misrepresent the actual combined inflow when peaks arrive at different times. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Catchment runoff peak” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設集水區2 km²、C=0.75、雨強60 mm/h且歷時超過集流時間；Q=0.278CiA=25.02 m³/s，未含渠道滯蓄。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume area 2 km², C=0.75 and intensity 60 mm/h lasting beyond concentration time.","failure":"常見誤解：「各分區最大流量無須考慮時序就能直接相加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Subcatchment peak discharges can be added directly without considering their timing.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「集水區逕流峰值」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Catchment runoff peak”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-01-k1","title":"集水區逕流峰值","titleEn":"Catchment runoff peak","text":"都市不透水面提高快速逕流比例，但降雨空間與集流時間控制峰值。合理化公式適合指定的小型集水區條件，不能直接代表整個大型水庫入流歷線。","textEn":"Impervious surfaces increase rapid runoff, while rainfall distribution and concentration time control the peak. The rational method applies to specified small-catchment conditions, not a complete large-reservoir inflow hydrograph.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：各分區最大流量無須考慮時序就能直接相加。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Subcatchment peak discharges can be added directly without considering their timing. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「集水區逕流峰值」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Catchment runoff peak\" is correct?","options":["各分區最大流量無須考慮時序就能直接相加。","都市不透水面提高快速逕流比例，但降雨空間與集流時間控制峰值。","水庫水位不變就表示沒有大量水量流入與流出。"],"optionsEn":["Subcatchment peak discharges can be added directly without considering their timing.","Impervious surfaces increase rapid runoff, while rainfall distribution and concentration time control the peak.","An unchanged reservoir level means there is no substantial inflow or outflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"都市不透水面提高快速逕流比例，但降雨空間與集流時間控制峰值。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Impervious surfaces increase rapid runoff, while rainfall distribution and concentration time control the peak. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b225-v15-02","title":"集水區逕流峰值：定量估算","titleEn":"Catchment runoff peak: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「集水區逕流峰值」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Catchment runoff peak” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設集水區2 km²、C=0.75、雨強60 mm/h且歷時超過集流時間；Q=0.278CiA=25.02 m³/s，未含渠道滯蓄。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume area 2 km², C=0.75 and intensity 60 mm/h lasting beyond concentration time. Q=0.278CiA=25.02 m³/s, excluding channel storage. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用雨量站與雷達核對雨強是否覆蓋集水區，再比較出口流量和延遲；將土地利用變更、排水分區和所選集流時間附在計算表。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check rain-gauge and radar coverage, then compare outlet flow and lag.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設集水區2 km²、C=0.75、雨強60 mm/h且歷時超過集流時間；Q=0.278CiA=25.02 m³/s，未含渠道滯蓄。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume area 2 km², C=0.75 and intensity 60 mm/h lasting beyond concentration time. Q=0.278CiA=25.02 m³/s, excluding channel storage.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「集水區逕流峰值」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Catchment runoff peak\", which statement holds?","options":["抽水機已經運轉就表示一定達到額定排水流量。","沒有明顯噪音就足以證明吸水條件有足夠餘裕。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設集水區2 km²、C=0.75、雨強60 mm/h且歷時超過集流時間。"],"optionsEn":["A running pump necessarily delivers its rated drainage flow.","Absence of obvious noise proves sufficient suction-head margin.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume area 2 km², C=0.75 and intensity 60 mm/h lasting beyond concentration time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設集水區2 km²、C=0.75、雨強60 mm/h且歷時超過集流時間；Q=0.278CiA=25.02 m³/s，未含渠道滯蓄。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume area 2 km², C=0.75 and intensity 60 mm/h lasting beyond concentration time. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b225-v15-03","title":"集水區逕流峰值：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Catchment runoff peak: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「集水區逕流峰值」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Catchment runoff peak” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用雨量站與雷達核對雨強是否覆蓋集水區，再比較出口流量和延遲；將土地利用變更、排水分區和所選集流時間附在計算表。對雨量歷時與集流時間的比值作檢查，確認峰值公式沒有用在尚未全區貢獻的短雨。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check rain-gauge and radar coverage, then compare outlet flow and lag. Attach land-use changes, drainage boundaries and chosen concentration time to the calculation record. Compare storm duration with concentration time to ensure the peak formula is not applied before the full catchment contributes. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以集水區逕流峰值編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用雨量站與雷達核對雨強是否覆蓋集水區，再比較出口流量和延遲；將土地利用變更、排水分區和所選集流時間附在計算表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for catchment runoff peak, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check rain-gauge and radar coverage, then compare outlet flow and lag. Attach land-use changes, drainage boundaries and chosen concentration time to the calculation record.","failure":"注意干擾：短時局部暴雨可能不符合均勻降雨假設，排水瓶頸也會改變峰值時間。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Brief localized storms violate uniform rainfall assumptions, and drainage bottlenecks alter peak timing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用雨量站與雷達核對雨強是否覆蓋集水區，再比較出口流量和延遲；將土地利用變更、排水分區和所選集流時間附在計算表。對雨量歷時與集流時間的比值作檢查，確認峰值公式沒有用在尚未全區貢獻的短雨。","textEn":"Check rain-gauge and radar coverage, then compare outlet flow and lag. Attach land-use changes, drainage boundaries and chosen concentration time to the calculation record. Compare storm duration with concentration time to ensure the peak formula is not applied before the full catchment contributes.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以集水區逕流峰值編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用雨量站與雷達核對雨強是否覆蓋集水區，再比較出口流量和延遲；將土地利用變更、排水分區和所選集流時間附在計算表。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for catchment runoff peak, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check rain-gauge and radar coverage, then compare outlet flow and lag. Attach land-use changes, drainage boundaries and chosen concentration time to the calculation record.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「集水區逕流峰值」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Catchment runoff peak\"?","options":["用雨量站與雷達核對雨強是否覆蓋集水區，再比較出口流量和延遲；將土地利用變更、排水分區和所選集流時間附在計算表。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","縮短平均停留時間就能保證每個灣區都有效換水。"],"optionsEn":["Check rain-gauge and radar coverage, then compare outlet flow and lag.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Shorter mean residence guarantees effective renewal in every reservoir arm."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用雨量站與雷達核對雨強是否覆蓋集水區，再比較出口流量和延遲；將土地利用變更、排水分區和所選集流時間附在計算表。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check rain-gauge and radar coverage, then compare outlet flow and lag. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b225-v15-04","title":"集水區逕流峰值：失效診斷","titleEn":"Catchment runoff peak: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「集水區逕流峰值」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Catchment runoff peak” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"短時局部暴雨可能不符合均勻降雨假設，排水瓶頸也會改變峰值時間。把每個分區峰值直接相加，可能錯估各峰不同時到達的真實入流。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Brief localized storms violate uniform rainfall assumptions, and drainage bottlenecks alter peak timing. Adding every subcatchment peak directly can misrepresent the actual combined inflow when peaks arrive at different times. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把每個分區峰值直接相加，可能錯估各峰不同時到達的真實入流。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Adding every subcatchment peak directly can misrepresent the actual combined inflow when peaks arrive at different times.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「各分區最大流量無須考慮時序就能直接相加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Subcatchment peak discharges can be added directly without considering their timing.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"短時局部暴雨可能不符合均勻降雨假設，排水瓶頸也會改變峰值時間。把每個分區峰值直接相加，可能錯估各峰不同時到達的真實入流。","textEn":"Brief localized storms violate uniform rainfall assumptions, and drainage bottlenecks alter peak timing. Adding every subcatchment peak directly can misrepresent the actual combined inflow when peaks arrive at different times.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「集水區逕流峰值」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Catchment runoff peak\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","短時局部暴雨可能不符合均勻降雨假設，排水瓶頸也會改變峰值時間。","水庫水位不變就表示沒有大量水量流入與流出。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Brief localized storms violate uniform rainfall assumptions, and drainage bottlenecks alter peak timing.","An unchanged reservoir level means there is no substantial inflow or outflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"短時局部暴雨可能不符合均勻降雨假設，排水瓶頸也會改變峰值時間。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Brief localized storms violate uniform rainfall assumptions, and drainage bottlenecks alter peak timing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b225-v15-05","title":"庫容與淨入流：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Storage and net inflow: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「庫容與淨入流」如何影響新加坡濱海堤壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Storage and net inflow” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水庫水位變化由入流減去閘排、抽水及其他出流決定。庫面不是永遠固定，低窪岸帶開始淹沒時，水位與庫容的關係會改變。 假設淨入流80 m³/s持續30 min、有效水面3 km²，Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m；只作固定面積短時估算。 抽水流量若採額定值而非當時揚程下的實際值，會產生虛假的未量測入流。時間步太長又可能把短時高峰平滑掉，低估岸邊淹水機會。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「庫容與淨入流」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Reservoir level changes with inflow minus gravity discharge, pumping and other losses. Surface area is not always constant; inundating low banks changes the stage-storage relation. Assume net inflow 80 m³/s over thirty minutes and effective area 3 km². Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m, a short-duration constant-area estimate. Using rated pump discharge instead of flow at actual head creates false unexplained inflow. Long time steps smooth brief peaks and can underestimate opportunities for flooding along the reservoir edge. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Storage and net inflow” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設淨入流80 m³/s持續30 min、有效水面3 km²，Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m；只作固定面積短時估算。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume net inflow 80 m³/s over thirty minutes and effective area 3 km². Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m, a short-duration constant-area estimate.","failure":"常見誤解：「水庫水位不變就表示沒有大量水量流入與流出。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An unchanged reservoir level means there is no substantial inflow or outflow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「庫容與淨入流」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Storage and net inflow”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-05-k1","title":"庫容與淨入流","titleEn":"Storage and net inflow","text":"水庫水位變化由入流減去閘排、抽水及其他出流決定。庫面不是永遠固定，低窪岸帶開始淹沒時，水位與庫容的關係會改變。","textEn":"Reservoir level changes with inflow minus gravity discharge, pumping and other losses. Surface area is not always constant; inundating low banks changes the stage-storage relation.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水庫水位不變就表示沒有大量水量流入與流出。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An unchanged reservoir level means there is no substantial inflow or outflow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「庫容與淨入流」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Storage and net inflow\" is correct?","options":["水庫水位不變就表示沒有大量水量流入與流出。","平均庫位高於海面就保證所有瞬間都向海排水。","水庫水位變化由入流減去閘排、抽水及其他出流決定。"],"optionsEn":["An unchanged reservoir level means there is no substantial inflow or outflow.","A higher mean reservoir level guarantees outward flow at every instant.","Reservoir level changes with inflow minus gravity discharge, pumping and other losses."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水庫水位變化由入流減去閘排、抽水及其他出流決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Reservoir level changes with inflow minus gravity discharge, pumping and other losses. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b225-v15-06","title":"庫容與淨入流：定量估算","titleEn":"Storage and net inflow: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「庫容與淨入流」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Storage and net inflow” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設淨入流80 m³/s持續30 min、有效水面3 km²，Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m；只作固定面積短時估算。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume net inflow 80 m³/s over thirty minutes and effective area 3 km². Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m, a short-duration constant-area estimate. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將每個流量來源按相同時間步積分，對照實測庫容變化；檢查水位站是否受局部風浪或排水噴流影響，再辨認水量平衡殘差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Integrate each flow source on identical time steps and compare measured storage change.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設淨入流80 m³/s持續30 min、有效水面3 km²，Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m；只作固定面積短時估算。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume net inflow 80 m³/s over thirty minutes and effective area 3 km². Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m, a short-duration constant-area estimate.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「庫容與淨入流」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Storage and net inflow\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設淨入流80 m³/s持續30 min、有效水面3 km²，Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m；只作固定面積短時估算。","並聯兩台相同泵的總流量必定是單台的兩倍。","平均鹽度很低就表示所有深度的水質完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume net inflow 80 m³/s over thirty minutes and effective area 3 km². Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m, a short-duration constant-area estimate.","Two identical parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow.","Low mean salinity means water quality is identical at every depth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設淨入流80 m³/s持續30 min、有效水面3 km²，Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m；只作固定面積短時估算。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume net inflow 80 m³/s over thirty minutes and effective area 3 km². Δh=Qt/A=0.048 m, a short-duration constant-area estimate. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b225-v15-07","title":"庫容與淨入流：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Storage and net inflow: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「庫容與淨入流」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Storage and net inflow” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將每個流量來源按相同時間步積分，對照實測庫容變化；檢查水位站是否受局部風浪或排水噴流影響，再辨認水量平衡殘差。縮短積分時間步再做水量閉合，檢查估算最大水位是否隨解析度提高而穩定。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Integrate each flow source on identical time steps and compare measured storage change. Check gauges for local waves or discharge jets before interpreting the water-balance residual. Repeat storage closure with shorter integration steps and check whether maximum estimated level converges as resolution improves. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以庫容與淨入流編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。將每個流量來源按相同時間步積分，對照實測庫容變化；檢查水位站是否受局部風浪或排水噴流影響，再辨認水量平衡殘差。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for storage and net inflow, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Integrate each flow source on identical time steps and compare measured storage change. Check gauges for local waves or discharge jets before interpreting the water-balance residual.","failure":"注意干擾：抽水流量若採額定值而非當時揚程下的實際值，會產生虛假的未量測入流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using rated pump discharge instead of flow at actual head creates false unexplained inflow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將每個流量來源按相同時間步積分，對照實測庫容變化；檢查水位站是否受局部風浪或排水噴流影響，再辨認水量平衡殘差。縮短積分時間步再做水量閉合，檢查估算最大水位是否隨解析度提高而穩定。","textEn":"Integrate each flow source on identical time steps and compare measured storage change. Check gauges for local waves or discharge jets before interpreting the water-balance residual. Repeat storage closure with shorter integration steps and check whether maximum estimated level converges as resolution improves.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以庫容與淨入流編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。將每個流量來源按相同時間步積分，對照實測庫容變化；檢查水位站是否受局部風浪或排水噴流影響，再辨認水量平衡殘差。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for storage and net inflow, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Integrate each flow source on identical time steps and compare measured storage change. Check gauges for local waves or discharge jets before interpreting the water-balance residual.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「庫容與淨入流」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Storage and net inflow\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將每個流量來源按相同時間步積分，對照實測庫容變化；檢查水位站是否受局部風浪或排水噴流影響，再辨認水量平衡殘差。","差壓增加只可能來自攔污柵堵塞，與流量無關。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Integrate each flow source on identical time steps and compare measured storage change.","Higher screen differential head only indicates blockage and is unrelated to flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將每個流量來源按相同時間步積分，對照實測庫容變化；檢查水位站是否受局部風浪或排水噴流影響，再辨認水量平衡殘差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Integrate each flow source on identical time steps and compare measured storage change. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b225-v15-08","title":"庫容與淨入流：失效診斷","titleEn":"Storage and net inflow: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「庫容與淨入流」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Storage and net inflow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"抽水流量若採額定值而非當時揚程下的實際值，會產生虛假的未量測入流。時間步太長又可能把短時高峰平滑掉，低估岸邊淹水機會。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using rated pump discharge instead of flow at actual head creates false unexplained inflow. Long time steps smooth brief peaks and can underestimate opportunities for flooding along the reservoir edge. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：時間步太長又可能把短時高峰平滑掉，低估岸邊淹水機會。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Long time steps smooth brief peaks and can underestimate opportunities for flooding along the reservoir edge.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水庫水位不變就表示沒有大量水量流入與流出。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An unchanged reservoir level means there is no substantial inflow or outflow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"抽水流量若採額定值而非當時揚程下的實際值，會產生虛假的未量測入流。時間步太長又可能把短時高峰平滑掉，低估岸邊淹水機會。","textEn":"Using rated pump discharge instead of flow at actual head creates false unexplained inflow. Long time steps smooth brief peaks and can underestimate opportunities for flooding along the reservoir edge.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「庫容與淨入流」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Storage and net inflow\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","平均庫位高於海面就保證所有瞬間都向海排水。","抽水流量若採額定值而非當時揚程下的實際值，會產生虛假的未量測入流。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A higher mean reservoir level guarantees outward flow at every instant.","Using rated pump discharge instead of flow at actual head creates false unexplained inflow."],"answer":2,"explanation":"抽水流量若採額定值而非當時揚程下的實際值，會產生虛假的未量測入流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using rated pump discharge instead of flow at actual head creates false unexplained inflow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b225-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「低潮重力排水」與「高平均潮位抽水」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Low-tide gravity drainage\" and \"Pumping against elevated tide\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b225-v15-09","title":"低潮重力排水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Low-tide gravity drainage: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「低潮重力排水」如何影響新加坡濱海堤壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Low-tide gravity drainage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"庫水高於海水時可由水頭差驅動排水，潮位反轉則可能失去這項能力。閘口流況隨上下游淹沒程度改變，單一係數不能代表全部潮相。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設有效孔口20 m²、Cd=0.65、水頭差0.5 m；Q=CdA√(2gΔh)=40.72 m³/s，限淹沒孔口準穩定流。 水頭接近零時儀器偏差可能比真實差值更大，造成錯判流向。忽略海側波浪與回流時，即使平均水頭為正，也不能保證瞬間全向外排水。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「低潮重力排水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A positive reservoir-to-sea head can drive gravity drainage, but tidal reversal removes it. Opening hydraulics vary with downstream submergence, so one coefficient does not describe every tide. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume effective opening 20 m², Cd=0.65 and head difference 0.5 m. Q=CdA√(2gΔh)=40.72 m³/s, for quasi-steady submerged-orifice flow. Near zero head, instrument bias may exceed the real difference and reverse the inferred direction. Waves and return currents can create inward flow even with positive mean outward head. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Low-tide gravity drainage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「平均庫位高於海面就保證所有瞬間都向海排水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A higher mean reservoir level guarantees outward flow at every instant.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「低潮重力排水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Low-tide gravity drainage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-09-k1","title":"低潮重力排水","titleEn":"Low-tide gravity drainage","text":"庫水高於海水時可由水頭差驅動排水，潮位反轉則可能失去這項能力。閘口流況隨上下游淹沒程度改變，單一係數不能代表全部潮相。","textEn":"A positive reservoir-to-sea head can drive gravity drainage, but tidal reversal removes it. Opening hydraulics vary with downstream submergence, so one coefficient does not describe every tide.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均庫位高於海面就保證所有瞬間都向海排水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A higher mean reservoir level guarantees outward flow at every instant. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「低潮重力排水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Low-tide gravity drainage\" is correct?","options":["庫水高於海水時可由水頭差驅動排水，潮位反轉則可能失去這項能力。","平均庫位高於海面就保證所有瞬間都向海排水。","抽水機已經運轉就表示一定達到額定排水流量。"],"optionsEn":["A positive reservoir-to-sea head can drive gravity drainage, but tidal reversal removes it.","A higher mean reservoir level guarantees outward flow at every instant.","A running pump necessarily delivers its rated drainage flow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"庫水高於海水時可由水頭差驅動排水，潮位反轉則可能失去這項能力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A positive reservoir-to-sea head can drive gravity drainage, but tidal reversal removes it. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b225-v15-10","title":"低潮重力排水：定量估算","titleEn":"Low-tide gravity drainage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「低潮重力排水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Low-tide gravity drainage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設有效孔口20 m²、Cd=0.65、水頭差0.5 m；Q=CdA√(2gΔh)=40.72 m³/s，限淹沒孔口準穩定流。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume effective opening 20 m², Cd=0.65 and head difference 0.5 m. Q=CdA√(2gΔh)=40.72 m³/s, for quasi-steady submerged-orifice flow. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步核對內外水位、開口面積及流向，將資料分成淹沒與自由出流型態；以實測流量校正係數，並保留潮位快速變化期間的偏差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronize internal and external levels, opening area and flow direction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設有效孔口20 m²、Cd=0.65、水頭差0.5 m；Q=CdA√(2gΔh)=40.72 m³/s，限淹沒孔口準穩定流。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume effective opening 20 m², Cd=0.65 and head difference 0.5 m. Q=CdA√(2gΔh)=40.72 m³/s, for quasi-steady submerged-orifice flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「低潮重力排水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Low-tide gravity drainage\", which statement holds?","options":["沒有明顯噪音就足以證明吸水條件有足夠餘裕。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","縮短平均停留時間就能保證每個灣區都有效換水。"],"optionsEn":["Absence of obvious noise proves sufficient suction-head margin.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","Shorter mean residence guarantees effective renewal in every reservoir arm."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b225-v15-11","title":"低潮重力排水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Low-tide gravity drainage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「低潮重力排水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Low-tide gravity drainage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步核對內外水位、開口面積及流向，將資料分成淹沒與自由出流型態；以實測流量校正係數，並保留潮位快速變化期間的偏差。以雙向流量資料核對接近零水頭時的符號，量化水位零點偏差可能造成的判斷範圍。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronize internal and external levels, opening area and flow direction. Separate submerged and free-outflow regimes, calibrate coefficients with measured discharge and retain rapid-tide residuals. Check near-zero-head direction against bidirectional flow data and quantify the ambiguity caused by gauge-zero offsets. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以低潮重力排水編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。同步核對內外水位、開口面積及流向，將資料分成淹沒與自由出流型態；以實測流量校正係數，並保留潮位快速變化期間的偏差。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for low-tide gravity drainage, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Synchronize internal and external levels, opening area and flow direction. Separate submerged and free-outflow regimes, calibrate coefficients with measured discharge and retain rapid-tide residuals.","failure":"注意干擾：水頭接近零時儀器偏差可能比真實差值更大，造成錯判流向。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Near zero head, instrument bias may exceed the real difference and reverse the inferred direction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步核對內外水位、開口面積及流向，將資料分成淹沒與自由出流型態；以實測流量校正係數，並保留潮位快速變化期間的偏差。以雙向流量資料核對接近零水頭時的符號，量化水位零點偏差可能造成的判斷範圍。","textEn":"Synchronize internal and external levels, opening area and flow direction. Separate submerged and free-outflow regimes, calibrate coefficients with measured discharge and retain rapid-tide residuals. Check near-zero-head direction against bidirectional flow data and quantify the ambiguity caused by gauge-zero offsets.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以低潮重力排水編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。同步核對內外水位、開口面積及流向，將資料分成淹沒與自由出流型態；以實測流量校正係數，並保留潮位快速變化期間的偏差。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for low-tide gravity drainage, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Synchronize internal and external levels, opening area and flow direction. Separate submerged and free-outflow regimes, calibrate coefficients with measured discharge and retain rapid-tide residuals.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「低潮重力排水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Low-tide gravity drainage\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","罕見暴雨和罕見高潮可以不經檢查直接視為獨立。","同步核對內外水位、開口面積及流向，將資料分成淹沒與自由出流型態；以實測流量校正係數，並保留潮位快速變化期間的偏差。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Rare rainfall and rare high tides can be assumed independent without checking.","Synchronize internal and external levels, opening area and flow direction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步核對內外水位、開口面積及流向，將資料分成淹沒與自由出流型態；以實測流量校正係數，並保留潮位快速變化期間的偏差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronize internal and external levels, opening area and flow direction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b225-v15-12","title":"低潮重力排水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Low-tide gravity drainage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「低潮重力排水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Low-tide gravity drainage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"水頭接近零時儀器偏差可能比真實差值更大，造成錯判流向。忽略海側波浪與回流時，即使平均水頭為正，也不能保證瞬間全向外排水。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Near zero head, instrument bias may exceed the real difference and reverse the inferred direction. Waves and return currents can create inward flow even with positive mean outward head. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：忽略海側波浪與回流時，即使平均水頭為正，也不能保證瞬間全向外排水。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Waves and return currents can create inward flow even with positive mean outward head.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均庫位高於海面就保證所有瞬間都向海排水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A higher mean reservoir level guarantees outward flow at every instant.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"水頭接近零時儀器偏差可能比真實差值更大，造成錯判流向。忽略海側波浪與回流時，即使平均水頭為正，也不能保證瞬間全向外排水。","textEn":"Near zero head, instrument bias may exceed the real difference and reverse the inferred direction. Waves and return currents can create inward flow even with positive mean outward head.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「低潮重力排水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Low-tide gravity drainage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["水頭接近零時儀器偏差可能比真實差值更大，造成錯判流向。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","抽水機已經運轉就表示一定達到額定排水流量。"],"optionsEn":["Near zero head, instrument bias may exceed the real difference and reverse the inferred direction.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A running pump necessarily delivers its rated drainage flow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水頭接近零時儀器偏差可能比真實差值更大，造成錯判流向。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Near zero head, instrument bias may exceed the real difference and reverse the inferred direction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b225-v15-13","title":"高平均潮位抽水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pumping against elevated tide: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「高平均潮位抽水」如何影響新加坡濱海堤壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pumping against elevated tide” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"抽水把水量提升到較高海側水位，需要克服靜揚程和管路損失。功率隨流量與揚程變化，不能用固定每立方公尺能耗描述所有潮況。 取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。假設淡水Q=20 m³/s、總揚程3 m、總效率0.8；輸入P=ρgQH/η=735.75 kW，不含啟動電流或備援負載。 揚程增加可能使泵流量下降，同時改變效率與振動。只看設備已通電會高估排水能力；忽略輔助設備能耗也會低估整場暴雨的能源需求。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「高平均潮位抽水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pumping lifts water against sea level and conveyance losses. Power varies with both flow and head, so a fixed energy per cubic metre cannot describe all tidal conditions. Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Assume fresh-water flow 20 m³/s, total head 3 m and overall efficiency 0.8. Input P=ρgQH/η=735.75 kW, excluding starting current and auxiliary backup loads. Increasing head may reduce pump flow while changing efficiency and vibration. Energized equipment does not establish drainage capacity, and omitting auxiliary loads understates energy required for the complete storm event. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pumping against elevated tide” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「抽水機已經運轉就表示一定達到額定排水流量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A running pump necessarily delivers its rated drainage flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「高平均潮位抽水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pumping against elevated tide”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-13-k1","title":"高平均潮位抽水","titleEn":"Pumping against elevated tide","text":"抽水把水量提升到較高海側水位，需要克服靜揚程和管路損失。功率隨流量與揚程變化，不能用固定每立方公尺能耗描述所有潮況。","textEn":"Pumping lifts water against sea level and conveyance losses. Power varies with both flow and head, so a fixed energy per cubic metre cannot describe all tidal conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：抽水機已經運轉就表示一定達到額定排水流量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A running pump necessarily delivers its rated drainage flow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高平均潮位抽水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pumping against elevated tide\" is correct?","options":["抽水機已經運轉就表示一定達到額定排水流量。","抽水把水量提升到較高海側水位，需要克服靜揚程和管路損失。","並聯兩台相同泵的總流量必定是單台的兩倍。"],"optionsEn":["A running pump necessarily delivers its rated drainage flow.","Pumping lifts water against sea level and conveyance losses.","Two identical parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"抽水把水量提升到較高海側水位，需要克服靜揚程和管路損失。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pumping lifts water against sea level and conveyance losses. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b225-v15-14","title":"高平均潮位抽水：定量估算","titleEn":"Pumping against elevated tide: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「高平均潮位抽水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pumping against elevated tide” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。假設淡水Q=20 m³/s、總揚程3 m、總效率0.8；輸入P=ρgQH/η=735.75 kW，不含啟動電流或備援負載。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Assume fresh-water flow 20 m³/s, total head 3 m and overall efficiency 0.8. Input P=ρgQH/η=735.75 kW, excluding starting current and auxiliary backup loads. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對泵前後壓力、流量與電表，分列靜揚程和沿程損失；把效率對應到實際工況，不能以最佳效率點替代高海潮期間的效率。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare suction and delivery pressure, flow and metered electricity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。假設淡水Q=20 m³/s、總揚程3 m、總效率0.8；輸入P=ρgQH/η=735.75 kW，不含啟動電流或備援負載。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Assume fresh-water flow 20 m³/s, total head 3 m and overall efficiency 0.8. Input P=ρgQH/η=735.75 kW, excluding starting current and auxiliary backup loads.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高平均潮位抽水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pumping against elevated tide\", which statement holds?","options":["平均鹽度很低就表示所有深度的水質完全相同。","差壓增加只可能來自攔污柵堵塞，與流量無關。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。"],"optionsEn":["Low mean salinity means water quality is identical at every depth.","Higher screen differential head only indicates blockage and is unrelated to flow.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b225-v15-15","title":"高平均潮位抽水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pumping against elevated tide: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「高平均潮位抽水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pumping against elevated tide” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對泵前後壓力、流量與電表，分列靜揚程和沿程損失；把效率對應到實際工況，不能以最佳效率點替代高海潮期間的效率。以電功率扣除輔助負載後核對效率曲線，確認流量與揚程量測時間完全對齊。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare suction and delivery pressure, flow and metered electricity. Separate static head from line loss and use efficiency at the actual operating point rather than the best-efficiency value during high tide. Remove auxiliary electrical demand before checking efficiency curves and ensure head and discharge measurements are time-aligned. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以高平均潮位抽水編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對泵前後壓力、流量與電表，分列靜揚程和沿程損失；把效率對應到實際工況，不能以最佳效率點替代高海潮期間的效率。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for pumping against elevated tide, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare suction and delivery pressure, flow and metered electricity. Separate static head from line loss and use efficiency at the actual operating point rather than the best-efficiency value during high tide.","failure":"注意干擾：揚程增加可能使泵流量下降，同時改變效率與振動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Increasing head may reduce pump flow while changing efficiency and vibration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對泵前後壓力、流量與電表，分列靜揚程和沿程損失；把效率對應到實際工況，不能以最佳效率點替代高海潮期間的效率。以電功率扣除輔助負載後核對效率曲線，確認流量與揚程量測時間完全對齊。","textEn":"Compare suction and delivery pressure, flow and metered electricity. Separate static head from line loss and use efficiency at the actual operating point rather than the best-efficiency value during high tide. Remove auxiliary electrical demand before checking efficiency curves and ensure head and discharge measurements are time-aligned.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以高平均潮位抽水編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對泵前後壓力、流量與電表，分列靜揚程和沿程損失；把效率對應到實際工況，不能以最佳效率點替代高海潮期間的效率。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for pumping against elevated tide, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare suction and delivery pressure, flow and metered electricity. Separate static head from line loss and use efficiency at the actual operating point rather than the best-efficiency value during high tide.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高平均潮位抽水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pumping against elevated tide\"?","options":["核對泵前後壓力、流量與電表，分列靜揚程和沿程損失；把效率對應到實際工況，不能以最佳效率點替代高海潮期間的效率。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","各分區最大流量無須考慮時序就能直接相加。"],"optionsEn":["Compare suction and delivery pressure, flow and metered electricity.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Subcatchment peak discharges can be added directly without considering their timing."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對泵前後壓力、流量與電表，分列靜揚程和沿程損失；把效率對應到實際工況，不能以最佳效率點替代高海潮期間的效率。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare suction and delivery pressure, flow and metered electricity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b225-v15-16","title":"高平均潮位抽水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pumping against elevated tide: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「高平均潮位抽水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pumping against elevated tide” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"揚程增加可能使泵流量下降，同時改變效率與振動。只看設備已通電會高估排水能力；忽略輔助設備能耗也會低估整場暴雨的能源需求。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Increasing head may reduce pump flow while changing efficiency and vibration. Energized equipment does not establish drainage capacity, and omitting auxiliary loads understates energy required for the complete storm event. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只看設備已通電會高估排水能力；忽略輔助設備能耗也會低估整場暴雨的能源需求。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Energized equipment does not establish drainage capacity, and omitting auxiliary loads understates energy required for the complete storm event.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「抽水機已經運轉就表示一定達到額定排水流量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A running pump necessarily delivers its rated drainage flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"揚程增加可能使泵流量下降，同時改變效率與振動。只看設備已通電會高估排水能力；忽略輔助設備能耗也會低估整場暴雨的能源需求。","textEn":"Increasing head may reduce pump flow while changing efficiency and vibration. Energized equipment does not establish drainage capacity, and omitting auxiliary loads understates energy required for the complete storm event.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高平均潮位抽水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pumping against elevated tide\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","揚程增加可能使泵流量下降，同時改變效率與振動。","並聯兩台相同泵的總流量必定是單台的兩倍。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Increasing head may reduce pump flow while changing efficiency and vibration.","Two identical parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"揚程增加可能使泵流量下降，同時改變效率與振動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Increasing head may reduce pump flow while changing efficiency and vibration. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b225-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「並聯泵與系統曲線」與「汽蝕餘裕與吸水」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Parallel pumps and system curve\" and \"Cavitation margin and suction\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b225-v15-17","title":"並聯泵與系統曲線：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Parallel pumps and system curve: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「並聯泵與系統曲線」如何影響新加坡濱海堤壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Parallel pumps and system curve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"並聯泵共享同一出水系統，增加機組會提高管損，單機工作點也移動。因此兩台流量不是把單台自由出水流量直接相加。 曲線採H以m、q與Q以m³/s表示；截距10、2的單位為m，係數0.01、0.005的單位均為s²/m⁵。假設單泵H=10−0.01q²、系統H=2+0.005Q²，兩泵相同且Q=2q；解得Q=√(8/0.0075)=32.66 m³/s。 兩台老化程度不同會造成不均分流，甚至低流量機組接近不穩定區。忽略共用管損的加倍估算，通常會高估新增泵帶來的容量提升。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「並聯泵與系統曲線」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Parallel pumps share a discharge system. Adding units increases losses and shifts each operating point, so combined flow is not simply twice a single pump free-discharge rate. For these dimensional curves H is in m and q and Q are in m³/s. Intercepts 10 and 2 have units m; coefficients 0.01 and 0.005 both have units s²/m⁵. Assume each pump H=10−0.01q² and system H=2+0.005Q², with two identical pumps Q=2q. Solving gives Q=√(8/0.0075)=32.66 m³/s. Unequal ageing creates unequal sharing and may place one unit near an unstable low-flow region. Doubling capacity while ignoring shared losses typically overstates the benefit of adding another pump. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Parallel pumps and system curve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：曲線採H以m、q與Q以m³/s表示；截距10、2的單位為m，係數0.01、0.005的單位均為s²/m⁵。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: For these dimensional curves H is in m and q and Q are in m³/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「並聯兩台相同泵的總流量必定是單台的兩倍。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two identical parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「並聯泵與系統曲線」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Parallel pumps and system curve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-17-k1","title":"並聯泵與系統曲線","titleEn":"Parallel pumps and system curve","text":"並聯泵共享同一出水系統，增加機組會提高管損，單機工作點也移動。因此兩台流量不是把單台自由出水流量直接相加。","textEn":"Parallel pumps share a discharge system. Adding units increases losses and shifts each operating point, so combined flow is not simply twice a single pump free-discharge rate.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：並聯兩台相同泵的總流量必定是單台的兩倍。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two identical parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「並聯泵與系統曲線」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Parallel pumps and system curve\" is correct?","options":["並聯兩台相同泵的總流量必定是單台的兩倍。","沒有明顯噪音就足以證明吸水條件有足夠餘裕。","並聯泵共享同一出水系統，增加機組會提高管損，單機工作點也移動。"],"optionsEn":["Two identical parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow.","Absence of obvious noise proves sufficient suction-head margin.","Parallel pumps share a discharge system."],"answer":2,"explanation":"並聯泵共享同一出水系統，增加機組會提高管損，單機工作點也移動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Parallel pumps share a discharge system. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b225-v15-18","title":"並聯泵與系統曲線：定量估算","titleEn":"Parallel pumps and system curve: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「並聯泵與系統曲線」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Parallel pumps and system curve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：曲線採H以m、q與Q以m³/s表示；截距10、2的單位為m，係數0.01、0.005的單位均為s²/m⁵。假設單泵H=10−0.01q²、系統H=2+0.005Q²，兩泵相同且Q=2q；解得Q=√(8/0.0075)=32.66 m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: For these dimensional curves H is in m and q and Q are in m³/s. Intercepts 10 and 2 have units m; coefficients 0.01 and 0.005 both have units s²/m⁵. Assume each pump H=10−0.01q² and system H=2+0.005Q², with two identical pumps Q=2q. Solving gives Q=√(8/0.0075)=32.66 m³/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將單泵曲線換成共同總流量座標，與系統曲線交點比較實測揚程；逐台核對流量分配與逆止閥狀態，避免只看總出水量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Convert individual pump curves to a common total-flow axis and compare the intersection with measured head.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：曲線採H以m、q與Q以m³/s表示；截距10、2的單位為m，係數0.01、0.005的單位均為s²/m⁵。假設單泵H=10−0.01q²、系統H=2+0.005Q²，兩泵相同且Q=2q；解得Q=√(8/0.0075)=32.66 m³/s。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: For these dimensional curves H is in m and q and Q are in m³/s. Intercepts 10 and 2 have units m; coefficients 0.01 and 0.005 both have units s²/m⁵. Assume each pump H=10−0.01q² and system H=2+0.005Q², with two identical pumps Q=2q. Solving gives Q=√(8/0.0075)=32.66 m³/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「並聯泵與系統曲線」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Parallel pumps and system curve\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：曲線採H以m、q與Q以m³/s表示；截距10、2的單位為m，係數0.01、0.005的單位均為s²/m⁵。","縮短平均停留時間就能保證每個灣區都有效換水。","罕見暴雨和罕見高潮可以不經檢查直接視為獨立。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: For these dimensional curves H is in m and q and Q are in m³/s.","Shorter mean residence guarantees effective renewal in every reservoir arm.","Rare rainfall and rare high tides can be assumed independent without checking."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：曲線採H以m、q與Q以m³/s表示；截距10、2的單位為m，係數0.01、0.005的單位均為s²/m⁵。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: For these dimensional curves H is in m and q and Q are in m³/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b225-v15-19","title":"並聯泵與系統曲線：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Parallel pumps and system curve: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「並聯泵與系統曲線」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Parallel pumps and system curve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將單泵曲線換成共同總流量座標，與系統曲線交點比較實測揚程；逐台核對流量分配與逆止閥狀態，避免只看總出水量。以逐台投入的穩定工況重建系統阻力係數，檢查兩台流量分配是否符合各自泵曲線。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Convert individual pump curves to a common total-flow axis and compare the intersection with measured head. Check individual sharing and check-valve behavior instead of relying only on total discharge. Reconstruct system resistance from staged steady operation and check each pump share against its own performance curve. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以並聯泵與系統曲線編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。將單泵曲線換成共同總流量座標，與系統曲線交點比較實測揚程；逐台核對流量分配與逆止閥狀態，避免只看總出水量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for parallel pumps and system curve, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Convert individual pump curves to a common total-flow axis and compare the intersection with measured head. Check individual sharing and check-valve behavior instead of relying only on total discharge.","failure":"注意干擾：兩台老化程度不同會造成不均分流，甚至低流量機組接近不穩定區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unequal ageing creates unequal sharing and may place one unit near an unstable low-flow region. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將單泵曲線換成共同總流量座標，與系統曲線交點比較實測揚程；逐台核對流量分配與逆止閥狀態，避免只看總出水量。以逐台投入的穩定工況重建系統阻力係數，檢查兩台流量分配是否符合各自泵曲線。","textEn":"Convert individual pump curves to a common total-flow axis and compare the intersection with measured head. Check individual sharing and check-valve behavior instead of relying only on total discharge. Reconstruct system resistance from staged steady operation and check each pump share against its own performance curve.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以並聯泵與系統曲線編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。將單泵曲線換成共同總流量座標，與系統曲線交點比較實測揚程；逐台核對流量分配與逆止閥狀態，避免只看總出水量。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for parallel pumps and system curve, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Convert individual pump curves to a common total-flow axis and compare the intersection with measured head. Check individual sharing and check-valve behavior instead of relying only on total discharge.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「並聯泵與系統曲線」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Parallel pumps and system curve\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","將單泵曲線換成共同總流量座標，與系統曲線交點比較實測揚程；逐台核對流量分配與逆止閥狀態，避免只看總出水量。","水庫水位不變就表示沒有大量水量流入與流出。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Convert individual pump curves to a common total-flow axis and compare the intersection with measured head.","An unchanged reservoir level means there is no substantial inflow or outflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將單泵曲線換成共同總流量座標，與系統曲線交點比較實測揚程；逐台核對流量分配與逆止閥狀態，避免只看總出水量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Convert individual pump curves to a common total-flow axis and compare the intersection with measured head. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b225-v15-20","title":"並聯泵與系統曲線：失效診斷","titleEn":"Parallel pumps and system curve: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「並聯泵與系統曲線」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Parallel pumps and system curve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩台老化程度不同會造成不均分流，甚至低流量機組接近不穩定區。忽略共用管損的加倍估算，通常會高估新增泵帶來的容量提升。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unequal ageing creates unequal sharing and may place one unit near an unstable low-flow region. Doubling capacity while ignoring shared losses typically overstates the benefit of adding another pump. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：忽略共用管損的加倍估算，通常會高估新增泵帶來的容量提升。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Doubling capacity while ignoring shared losses typically overstates the benefit of adding another pump.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「並聯兩台相同泵的總流量必定是單台的兩倍。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two identical parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩台老化程度不同會造成不均分流，甚至低流量機組接近不穩定區。忽略共用管損的加倍估算，通常會高估新增泵帶來的容量提升。","textEn":"Unequal ageing creates unequal sharing and may place one unit near an unstable low-flow region. Doubling capacity while ignoring shared losses typically overstates the benefit of adding another pump.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「並聯泵與系統曲線」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Parallel pumps and system curve\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","沒有明顯噪音就足以證明吸水條件有足夠餘裕。","兩台老化程度不同會造成不均分流，甚至低流量機組接近不穩定區。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Absence of obvious noise proves sufficient suction-head margin.","Unequal ageing creates unequal sharing and may place one unit near an unstable low-flow region."],"answer":2,"explanation":"兩台老化程度不同會造成不均分流，甚至低流量機組接近不穩定區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unequal ageing creates unequal sharing and may place one unit near an unstable low-flow region. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b225-v15-21","title":"汽蝕餘裕與吸水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cavitation margin and suction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「汽蝕餘裕與吸水」如何影響新加坡濱海堤壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cavitation margin and suction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"吸水側壓力若接近水的汽化壓，氣泡形成與崩潰會傷害葉片。淨正吸入水頭需使用絕對壓力，且和廠商所定試驗條件分開比較。 假設大氣水頭10.3 m、吸水靜高1.5 m、吸管損失0.8 m、汽化水頭0.3 m，NPSHa=10.3+1.5−0.8−0.3=10.7 m。 低水位與堵塞會同時降低可用吸入水頭，吸入空氣也會產生類似汽蝕的噪音。以冷水汽化壓代表熱天水況，可能誇大實際餘裕。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「汽蝕餘裕與吸水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Vapor bubbles form and collapse when suction pressure approaches vapor pressure, damaging impellers. Available net positive suction head uses absolute pressure and must be compared with the manufacturer test definition. Assume atmospheric head 10.3 m, positive suction static head 1.5 m, suction loss 0.8 m and vapor head 0.3 m. NPSHa=10.3+1.5−0.8−0.3=10.7 m. Low level and blockage both reduce available suction head, while entrained air can imitate cavitation noise. Using cold-water vapor pressure for warm conditions may exaggerate the available margin. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cavitation margin and suction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設大氣水頭10.3 m、吸水靜高1.5 m、吸管損失0.8 m、汽化水頭0.3 m，NPSHa=10.3+1.5−0.8−0.3=10.7 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume atmospheric head 10.3 m, positive suction static head 1.5 m, suction loss 0.8 m and vapor head 0.3 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「沒有明顯噪音就足以證明吸水條件有足夠餘裕。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Absence of obvious noise proves sufficient suction-head margin.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「汽蝕餘裕與吸水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cavitation margin and suction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-21-k1","title":"汽蝕餘裕與吸水","titleEn":"Cavitation margin and suction","text":"吸水側壓力若接近水的汽化壓，氣泡形成與崩潰會傷害葉片。淨正吸入水頭需使用絕對壓力，且和廠商所定試驗條件分開比較。","textEn":"Vapor bubbles form and collapse when suction pressure approaches vapor pressure, damaging impellers. Available net positive suction head uses absolute pressure and must be compared with the manufacturer test definition.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：沒有明顯噪音就足以證明吸水條件有足夠餘裕。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Absence of obvious noise proves sufficient suction-head margin. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「汽蝕餘裕與吸水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cavitation margin and suction\" is correct?","options":["吸水側壓力若接近水的汽化壓，氣泡形成與崩潰會傷害葉片。","沒有明顯噪音就足以證明吸水條件有足夠餘裕。","平均鹽度很低就表示所有深度的水質完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Vapor bubbles form and collapse when suction pressure approaches vapor pressure, damaging impellers.","Absence of obvious noise proves sufficient suction-head margin.","Low mean salinity means water quality is identical at every depth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"吸水側壓力若接近水的汽化壓，氣泡形成與崩潰會傷害葉片。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Vapor bubbles form and collapse when suction pressure approaches vapor pressure, damaging impellers. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b225-v15-22","title":"汽蝕餘裕與吸水：定量估算","titleEn":"Cavitation margin and suction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「汽蝕餘裕與吸水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cavitation margin and suction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設大氣水頭10.3 m、吸水靜高1.5 m、吸管損失0.8 m、汽化水頭0.3 m，NPSHa=10.3+1.5−0.8−0.3=10.7 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume atmospheric head 10.3 m, positive suction static head 1.5 m, suction loss 0.8 m and vapor head 0.3 m. NPSHa=10.3+1.5−0.8−0.3=10.7 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：記錄水溫、水位與吸口壓力，核對入口旋渦和攔污柵堵塞；將振動、噪音與效率變化一起判讀，避免把任一聲音直接認定為汽蝕。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record temperature, water level and suction pressure, checking intake vortices and screen blockage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設大氣水頭10.3 m、吸水靜高1.5 m、吸管損失0.8 m、汽化水頭0.3 m，NPSHa=10.3+1.5−0.8−0.3=10.7 m。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume atmospheric head 10.3 m, positive suction static head 1.5 m, suction loss 0.8 m and vapor head 0.3 m. NPSHa=10.3+1.5−0.8−0.3=10.7 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「汽蝕餘裕與吸水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cavitation margin and suction\", which statement holds?","options":["差壓增加只可能來自攔污柵堵塞，與流量無關。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設大氣水頭10.3 m、吸水靜高1.5 m、吸管損失0.8 m、汽化水頭0.3 m，NPSHa=10.3+1.5−0.8−0.3=10.7 m。","各分區最大流量無須考慮時序就能直接相加。"],"optionsEn":["Higher screen differential head only indicates blockage and is unrelated to flow.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume atmospheric head 10.3 m, positive suction static head 1.5 m, suction loss 0.8 m and vapor head 0.3 m.","Subcatchment peak discharges can be added directly without considering their timing."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設大氣水頭10.3 m、吸水靜高1.5 m、吸管損失0.8 m、汽化水頭0.3 m，NPSHa=10.3+1.5−0.8−0.3=10.7 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume atmospheric head 10.3 m, positive suction static head 1.5 m, suction loss 0.8 m and vapor head 0.3 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b225-v15-23","title":"汽蝕餘裕與吸水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cavitation margin and suction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「汽蝕餘裕與吸水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cavitation margin and suction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"記錄水溫、水位與吸口壓力，核對入口旋渦和攔污柵堵塞；將振動、噪音與效率變化一起判讀，避免把任一聲音直接認定為汽蝕。將最低吸水位和最高水溫的證據並列，確認吸入空氣與汽化空泡已用不同訊號辨識。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record temperature, water level and suction pressure, checking intake vortices and screen blockage. Interpret vibration, noise and efficiency together instead of identifying cavitation from sound alone. Compare minimum suction level with maximum water temperature and distinguish entrained air from vapor cavities using separate evidence. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以汽蝕餘裕與吸水編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。記錄水溫、水位與吸口壓力，核對入口旋渦和攔污柵堵塞；將振動、噪音與效率變化一起判讀，避免把任一聲音直接認定為汽蝕。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for cavitation margin and suction, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Record temperature, water level and suction pressure, checking intake vortices and screen blockage. Interpret vibration, noise and efficiency together instead of identifying cavitation from sound alone.","failure":"注意干擾：低水位與堵塞會同時降低可用吸入水頭，吸入空氣也會產生類似汽蝕的噪音。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Low level and blockage both reduce available suction head, while entrained air can imitate cavitation noise. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"記錄水溫、水位與吸口壓力，核對入口旋渦和攔污柵堵塞；將振動、噪音與效率變化一起判讀，避免把任一聲音直接認定為汽蝕。將最低吸水位和最高水溫的證據並列，確認吸入空氣與汽化空泡已用不同訊號辨識。","textEn":"Record temperature, water level and suction pressure, checking intake vortices and screen blockage. Interpret vibration, noise and efficiency together instead of identifying cavitation from sound alone. Compare minimum suction level with maximum water temperature and distinguish entrained air from vapor cavities using separate evidence.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以汽蝕餘裕與吸水編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。記錄水溫、水位與吸口壓力，核對入口旋渦和攔污柵堵塞；將振動、噪音與效率變化一起判讀，避免把任一聲音直接認定為汽蝕。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for cavitation margin and suction, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Record temperature, water level and suction pressure, checking intake vortices and screen blockage. Interpret vibration, noise and efficiency together instead of identifying cavitation from sound alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「汽蝕餘裕與吸水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cavitation margin and suction\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","平均庫位高於海面就保證所有瞬間都向海排水。","記錄水溫、水位與吸口壓力，核對入口旋渦和攔污柵堵塞；將振動、噪音與效率變化一起判讀，避免把任一聲音直接認定為汽蝕。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A higher mean reservoir level guarantees outward flow at every instant.","Record temperature, water level and suction pressure, checking intake vortices and screen blockage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"記錄水溫、水位與吸口壓力，核對入口旋渦和攔污柵堵塞；將振動、噪音與效率變化一起判讀，避免把任一聲音直接認定為汽蝕。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record temperature, water level and suction pressure, checking intake vortices and screen blockage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b225-v15-24","title":"汽蝕餘裕與吸水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cavitation margin and suction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「汽蝕餘裕與吸水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cavitation margin and suction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"低水位與堵塞會同時降低可用吸入水頭，吸入空氣也會產生類似汽蝕的噪音。以冷水汽化壓代表熱天水況，可能誇大實際餘裕。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Low level and blockage both reduce available suction head, while entrained air can imitate cavitation noise. Using cold-water vapor pressure for warm conditions may exaggerate the available margin. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以冷水汽化壓代表熱天水況，可能誇大實際餘裕。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Using cold-water vapor pressure for warm conditions may exaggerate the available margin.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「沒有明顯噪音就足以證明吸水條件有足夠餘裕。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Absence of obvious noise proves sufficient suction-head margin.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"低水位與堵塞會同時降低可用吸入水頭，吸入空氣也會產生類似汽蝕的噪音。以冷水汽化壓代表熱天水況，可能誇大實際餘裕。","textEn":"Low level and blockage both reduce available suction head, while entrained air can imitate cavitation noise. Using cold-water vapor pressure for warm conditions may exaggerate the available margin.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「汽蝕餘裕與吸水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cavitation margin and suction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["低水位與堵塞會同時降低可用吸入水頭，吸入空氣也會產生類似汽蝕的噪音。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","平均鹽度很低就表示所有深度的水質完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Low level and blockage both reduce available suction head, while entrained air can imitate cavitation noise.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Low mean salinity means water quality is identical at every depth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"低水位與堵塞會同時降低可用吸入水頭，吸入空氣也會產生類似汽蝕的噪音。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Low level and blockage both reduce available suction head, while entrained air can imitate cavitation noise. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b225-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「鹽水入侵質量平衡」與「水力停留與營養鹽」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Salt intrusion mass balance\" and \"Residence time and nutrients\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b225-v15-25","title":"鹽水入侵質量平衡：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Salt intrusion mass balance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「鹽水入侵質量平衡」如何影響新加坡濱海堤壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Salt intrusion mass balance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"淡水庫的鹽度受微量海水入侵影響，鹽水密度較大會先沿底部擴散。平均混合模型只能估算總鹽量，不能代表取水口短時濃度。 假設淡水體積1 million m³、混入1000 m³海水鹽度35 g/kg，同密度完全混合；平均鹽度35×1000/1001000=0.03497 g/kg。 稀釋後平均值很低仍可能有高鹽舌接近取水口，風浪混合也可能突然把底水抬升。只在表層採樣，會誤認鹽水已完全排除。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鹽水入侵質量平衡」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Small seawater intrusions affect a freshwater reservoir, and denser water can spread along the bottom first. A mean-mixing model estimates total salt but not short-term intake concentration. Assume freshwater volume 1 million m³ and intrusion 1000 m³ at 35 g/kg, equal densities and complete mixing. Mean salinity is 35×1000/1001000=0.03497 g/kg. A low diluted mean can coexist with a saline tongue near an intake. Wind mixing may suddenly lift bottom water, while surface-only sampling can falsely suggest intrusion has been removed. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Salt intrusion mass balance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設淡水體積1 million m³、混入1000 m³海水鹽度35 g/kg，同密度完全混合；平均鹽度35×1000/1001000=0.03497 g/kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume freshwater volume 1 million m³ and intrusion 1000 m³ at 35 g/kg, equal densities and complete mixing.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均鹽度很低就表示所有深度的水質完全相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Low mean salinity means water quality is identical at every depth.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鹽水入侵質量平衡」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Salt intrusion mass balance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-25-k1","title":"鹽水入侵質量平衡","titleEn":"Salt intrusion mass balance","text":"淡水庫的鹽度受微量海水入侵影響，鹽水密度較大會先沿底部擴散。平均混合模型只能估算總鹽量，不能代表取水口短時濃度。","textEn":"Small seawater intrusions affect a freshwater reservoir, and denser water can spread along the bottom first. A mean-mixing model estimates total salt but not short-term intake concentration.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均鹽度很低就表示所有深度的水質完全相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Low mean salinity means water quality is identical at every depth. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鹽水入侵質量平衡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Salt intrusion mass balance\" is correct?","options":["平均鹽度很低就表示所有深度的水質完全相同。","淡水庫的鹽度受微量海水入侵影響，鹽水密度較大會先沿底部擴散。","縮短平均停留時間就能保證每個灣區都有效換水。"],"optionsEn":["Low mean salinity means water quality is identical at every depth.","Small seawater intrusions affect a freshwater reservoir, and denser water can spread along the bottom first.","Shorter mean residence guarantees effective renewal in every reservoir arm."],"answer":1,"explanation":"淡水庫的鹽度受微量海水入侵影響，鹽水密度較大會先沿底部擴散。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Small seawater intrusions affect a freshwater reservoir, and denser water can spread along the bottom first. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b225-v15-26","title":"鹽水入侵質量平衡：定量估算","titleEn":"Salt intrusion mass balance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鹽水入侵質量平衡」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Salt intrusion mass balance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設淡水體積1 million m³、混入1000 m³海水鹽度35 g/kg，同密度完全混合；平均鹽度35×1000/1001000=0.03497 g/kg。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume freshwater volume 1 million m³ and intrusion 1000 m³ at 35 g/kg, equal densities and complete mixing. Mean salinity is 35×1000/1001000=0.03497 g/kg. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿庫底至取水口布設深度剖面，校正電導與溫度，再以水量平衡核對入侵總量；保留底層尖峰而非只輸出全庫平均。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Profile depth from the bed to the intake, calibrating conductivity and temperature.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設淡水體積1 million m³、混入1000 m³海水鹽度35 g/kg，同密度完全混合；平均鹽度35×1000/1001000=0.03497 g/kg。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume freshwater volume 1 million m³ and intrusion 1000 m³ at 35 g/kg, equal densities and complete mixing. Mean salinity is 35×1000/1001000=0.03497 g/kg.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鹽水入侵質量平衡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Salt intrusion mass balance\", which statement holds?","options":["罕見暴雨和罕見高潮可以不經檢查直接視為獨立。","水庫水位不變就表示沒有大量水量流入與流出。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設淡水體積1 million m³、混入1000 m³海水鹽度35 g/kg，同密度完全混合。"],"optionsEn":["Rare rainfall and rare high tides can be assumed independent without checking.","An unchanged reservoir level means there is no substantial inflow or outflow.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume freshwater volume 1 million m³ and intrusion 1000 m³ at 35 g/kg, equal densities and complete mixing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設淡水體積1 million m³、混入1000 m³海水鹽度35 g/kg，同密度完全混合；平均鹽度35×1000/1001000=0.03497 g/kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume freshwater volume 1 million m³ and intrusion 1000 m³ at 35 g/kg, equal densities and complete mixing. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b225-v15-27","title":"鹽水入侵質量平衡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Salt intrusion mass balance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鹽水入侵質量平衡」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Salt intrusion mass balance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿庫底至取水口布設深度剖面，校正電導與溫度，再以水量平衡核對入侵總量；保留底層尖峰而非只輸出全庫平均。用底層鹽度時序估算前緣移動，核對取水口短時峰值是否被全庫平均值掩蓋。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Profile depth from the bed to the intake, calibrating conductivity and temperature. Check intrusion volume against water balance and preserve bottom-layer peaks rather than reporting only a reservoir average. Estimate front movement from bottom-salinity histories and check whether the reservoir mean conceals brief intake peaks. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以鹽水入侵質量平衡編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。沿庫底至取水口布設深度剖面，校正電導與溫度，再以水量平衡核對入侵總量；保留底層尖峰而非只輸出全庫平均。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for salt intrusion mass balance, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Profile depth from the bed to the intake, calibrating conductivity and temperature. Check intrusion volume against water balance and preserve bottom-layer peaks rather than reporting only a reservoir average.","failure":"注意干擾：稀釋後平均值很低仍可能有高鹽舌接近取水口，風浪混合也可能突然把底水抬升。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A low diluted mean can coexist with a saline tongue near an intake. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿庫底至取水口布設深度剖面，校正電導與溫度，再以水量平衡核對入侵總量；保留底層尖峰而非只輸出全庫平均。用底層鹽度時序估算前緣移動，核對取水口短時峰值是否被全庫平均值掩蓋。","textEn":"Profile depth from the bed to the intake, calibrating conductivity and temperature. Check intrusion volume against water balance and preserve bottom-layer peaks rather than reporting only a reservoir average. Estimate front movement from bottom-salinity histories and check whether the reservoir mean conceals brief intake peaks.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以鹽水入侵質量平衡編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。沿庫底至取水口布設深度剖面，校正電導與溫度，再以水量平衡核對入侵總量；保留底層尖峰而非只輸出全庫平均。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for salt intrusion mass balance, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Profile depth from the bed to the intake, calibrating conductivity and temperature. Check intrusion volume against water balance and preserve bottom-layer peaks rather than reporting only a reservoir average.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鹽水入侵質量平衡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Salt intrusion mass balance\"?","options":["沿庫底至取水口布設深度剖面，校正電導與溫度，再以水量平衡核對入侵總量；保留底層尖峰而非只輸出全庫平均。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","抽水機已經運轉就表示一定達到額定排水流量。"],"optionsEn":["Profile depth from the bed to the intake, calibrating conductivity and temperature.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A running pump necessarily delivers its rated drainage flow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿庫底至取水口布設深度剖面，校正電導與溫度，再以水量平衡核對入侵總量；保留底層尖峰而非只輸出全庫平均。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Profile depth from the bed to the intake, calibrating conductivity and temperature. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b225-v15-28","title":"鹽水入侵質量平衡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Salt intrusion mass balance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鹽水入侵質量平衡」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Salt intrusion mass balance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"稀釋後平均值很低仍可能有高鹽舌接近取水口，風浪混合也可能突然把底水抬升。只在表層採樣，會誤認鹽水已完全排除。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A low diluted mean can coexist with a saline tongue near an intake. Wind mixing may suddenly lift bottom water, while surface-only sampling can falsely suggest intrusion has been removed. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只在表層採樣，會誤認鹽水已完全排除。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Wind mixing may suddenly lift bottom water, while surface-only sampling can falsely suggest intrusion has been removed.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均鹽度很低就表示所有深度的水質完全相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Low mean salinity means water quality is identical at every depth.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"稀釋後平均值很低仍可能有高鹽舌接近取水口，風浪混合也可能突然把底水抬升。只在表層採樣，會誤認鹽水已完全排除。","textEn":"A low diluted mean can coexist with a saline tongue near an intake. Wind mixing may suddenly lift bottom water, while surface-only sampling can falsely suggest intrusion has been removed.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鹽水入侵質量平衡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Salt intrusion mass balance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","稀釋後平均值很低仍可能有高鹽舌接近取水口，風浪混合也可能突然把底水抬升。","縮短平均停留時間就能保證每個灣區都有效換水。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A low diluted mean can coexist with a saline tongue near an intake.","Shorter mean residence guarantees effective renewal in every reservoir arm."],"answer":1,"explanation":"稀釋後平均值很低仍可能有高鹽舌接近取水口，風浪混合也可能突然把底水抬升。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A low diluted mean can coexist with a saline tongue near an intake. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b225-v15-29","title":"水力停留與營養鹽：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Residence time and nutrients: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「水力停留與營養鹽」如何影響新加坡濱海堤壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Residence time and nutrients” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"停留時間影響營養鹽累積和藻類生長，但流動短路會讓部分水很快排出、其他水長期滯留。平均V/Q只是比較尺度，不能單獨預測生態反應。 假設有效庫容12 million m³、平均換水量6 m³/s，V/Q=2 million s=23.15 days；穩定完全混合近似，不代表所有水齡。 用總庫容忽略實際隔離死水區會誤判交換效率，增加出流也不必然沖走滯水。若未分離光照和水溫，不能把藻量變化全歸因於停留時間。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水力停留與營養鹽」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Residence time influences nutrients and algae, but short-circuiting releases some water quickly while other regions stagnate. Mean V/Q is a comparison scale, not a complete ecological prediction. Assume effective volume 12 million m³ and average exchange 6 m³/s. V/Q=2 million s=23.15 days, a steady complete-mixing approximation rather than every parcel age. Ignoring isolated stagnant zones misjudges exchange, and more outflow need not flush them. Without separating light and temperature, changes in algae cannot be attributed entirely to hydraulic residence time. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Residence time and nutrients” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效庫容12 million m³、平均換水量6 m³/s，V/Q=2 million s=23.15 days；穩定完全混合近似，不代表所有水齡。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective volume 12 million m³ and average exchange 6 m³/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「縮短平均停留時間就能保證每個灣區都有效換水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Shorter mean residence guarantees effective renewal in every reservoir arm.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水力停留與營養鹽」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Residence time and nutrients”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-29-k1","title":"水力停留與營養鹽","titleEn":"Residence time and nutrients","text":"停留時間影響營養鹽累積和藻類生長，但流動短路會讓部分水很快排出、其他水長期滯留。平均V/Q只是比較尺度，不能單獨預測生態反應。","textEn":"Residence time influences nutrients and algae, but short-circuiting releases some water quickly while other regions stagnate. Mean V/Q is a comparison scale, not a complete ecological prediction.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：縮短平均停留時間就能保證每個灣區都有效換水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Shorter mean residence guarantees effective renewal in every reservoir arm. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水力停留與營養鹽」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Residence time and nutrients\" is correct?","options":["縮短平均停留時間就能保證每個灣區都有效換水。","差壓增加只可能來自攔污柵堵塞，與流量無關。","停留時間影響營養鹽累積和藻類生長，但流動短路會讓部分水很快排出、其他水長期滯留。"],"optionsEn":["Shorter mean residence guarantees effective renewal in every reservoir arm.","Higher screen differential head only indicates blockage and is unrelated to flow.","Residence time influences nutrients and algae, but short-circuiting releases some water quickly while other regions stagnate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"停留時間影響營養鹽累積和藻類生長，但流動短路會讓部分水很快排出、其他水長期滯留。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Residence time influences nutrients and algae, but short-circuiting releases some water quickly while other regions stagnate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b225-v15-30","title":"水力停留與營養鹽：定量估算","titleEn":"Residence time and nutrients: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水力停留與營養鹽」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Residence time and nutrients” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效庫容12 million m³、平均換水量6 m³/s，V/Q=2 million s=23.15 days；穩定完全混合近似，不代表所有水齡。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective volume 12 million m³ and average exchange 6 m³/s. V/Q=2 million s=23.15 days, a steady complete-mixing approximation rather than every parcel age. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以示蹤或導電度事件比較不同灣區到達時間，連同溶氧、溫度和葉綠素建立時序；區分物理滯留與外部營養鹽負荷增加。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare tracer or conductivity-event arrival times across reservoir arms and build oxygen, temperature and chlorophyll histories.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效庫容12 million m³、平均換水量6 m³/s，V/Q=2 million s=23.15 days；穩定完全混合近似，不代表所有水齡。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective volume 12 million m³ and average exchange 6 m³/s. V/Q=2 million s=23.15 days, a steady complete-mixing approximation rather than every parcel age.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水力停留與營養鹽」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Residence time and nutrients\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效庫容12 million m³、平均換水量6 m³/s，V/Q=2 million s=23.15 days。","各分區最大流量無須考慮時序就能直接相加。","平均庫位高於海面就保證所有瞬間都向海排水。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective volume 12 million m³ and average exchange 6 m³/s.","Subcatchment peak discharges can be added directly without considering their timing.","A higher mean reservoir level guarantees outward flow at every instant."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效庫容12 million m³、平均換水量6 m³/s，V/Q=2 million s=23.15 days；穩定完全混合近似，不代表所有水齡。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective volume 12 million m³ and average exchange 6 m³/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b225-v15-31","title":"水力停留與營養鹽：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Residence time and nutrients: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水力停留與營養鹽」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Residence time and nutrients” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以示蹤或導電度事件比較不同灣區到達時間，連同溶氧、溫度和葉綠素建立時序；區分物理滯留與外部營養鹽負荷增加。比較示蹤首達、峰值和尾跡時間，判斷短路流與長滯留區是否同時存在。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare tracer or conductivity-event arrival times across reservoir arms and build oxygen, temperature and chlorophyll histories. Distinguish physical retention from increased external nutrient loading. Compare tracer first arrival, peak and tail times to determine whether short-circuiting and long-retention regions coexist. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以水力停留與營養鹽編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以示蹤或導電度事件比較不同灣區到達時間，連同溶氧、溫度和葉綠素建立時序；區分物理滯留與外部營養鹽負荷增加。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for residence time and nutrients, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare tracer or conductivity-event arrival times across reservoir arms and build oxygen, temperature and chlorophyll histories. Distinguish physical retention from increased external nutrient loading.","failure":"注意干擾：用總庫容忽略實際隔離死水區會誤判交換效率，增加出流也不必然沖走滯水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring isolated stagnant zones misjudges exchange, and more outflow need not flush them. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以示蹤或導電度事件比較不同灣區到達時間，連同溶氧、溫度和葉綠素建立時序；區分物理滯留與外部營養鹽負荷增加。比較示蹤首達、峰值和尾跡時間，判斷短路流與長滯留區是否同時存在。","textEn":"Compare tracer or conductivity-event arrival times across reservoir arms and build oxygen, temperature and chlorophyll histories. Distinguish physical retention from increased external nutrient loading. Compare tracer first arrival, peak and tail times to determine whether short-circuiting and long-retention regions coexist.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以水力停留與營養鹽編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以示蹤或導電度事件比較不同灣區到達時間，連同溶氧、溫度和葉綠素建立時序；區分物理滯留與外部營養鹽負荷增加。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for residence time and nutrients, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare tracer or conductivity-event arrival times across reservoir arms and build oxygen, temperature and chlorophyll histories. Distinguish physical retention from increased external nutrient loading.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水力停留與營養鹽」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Residence time and nutrients\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以示蹤或導電度事件比較不同灣區到達時間，連同溶氧、溫度和葉綠素建立時序；區分物理滯留與外部營養鹽負荷增加。","並聯兩台相同泵的總流量必定是單台的兩倍。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare tracer or conductivity-event arrival times across reservoir arms and build oxygen, temperature and chlorophyll histories.","Two identical parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以示蹤或導電度事件比較不同灣區到達時間，連同溶氧、溫度和葉綠素建立時序；區分物理滯留與外部營養鹽負荷增加。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare tracer or conductivity-event arrival times across reservoir arms and build oxygen, temperature and chlorophyll histories. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b225-v15-32","title":"水力停留與營養鹽：失效診斷","titleEn":"Residence time and nutrients: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水力停留與營養鹽」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Residence time and nutrients” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用總庫容忽略實際隔離死水區會誤判交換效率，增加出流也不必然沖走滯水。若未分離光照和水溫，不能把藻量變化全歸因於停留時間。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring isolated stagnant zones misjudges exchange, and more outflow need not flush them. Without separating light and temperature, changes in algae cannot be attributed entirely to hydraulic residence time. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若未分離光照和水溫，不能把藻量變化全歸因於停留時間。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Without separating light and temperature, changes in algae cannot be attributed entirely to hydraulic residence time.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「縮短平均停留時間就能保證每個灣區都有效換水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Shorter mean residence guarantees effective renewal in every reservoir arm.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用總庫容忽略實際隔離死水區會誤判交換效率，增加出流也不必然沖走滯水。若未分離光照和水溫，不能把藻量變化全歸因於停留時間。","textEn":"Ignoring isolated stagnant zones misjudges exchange, and more outflow need not flush them. Without separating light and temperature, changes in algae cannot be attributed entirely to hydraulic residence time.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水力停留與營養鹽」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Residence time and nutrients\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","差壓增加只可能來自攔污柵堵塞，與流量無關。","用總庫容忽略實際隔離死水區會誤判交換效率，增加出流也不必然沖走滯水。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Higher screen differential head only indicates blockage and is unrelated to flow.","Ignoring isolated stagnant zones misjudges exchange, and more outflow need not flush them."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用總庫容忽略實際隔離死水區會誤判交換效率，增加出流也不必然沖走滯水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring isolated stagnant zones misjudges exchange, and more outflow need not flush them. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b225-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「攔污柵損失與堵塞」與「複合事件與失效組合」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Screen losses and blockage\" and \"Compound events and failure combinations\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b225-v15-33","title":"攔污柵損失與堵塞：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Screen losses and blockage: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「攔污柵損失與堵塞」如何影響新加坡濱海堤壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Screen losses and blockage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"攔污柵保護設備卻增加水頭損失，堵塞使有效流通面積縮小。損失係數與速度必須使用相容的面積定義，否則會重複計算堵塞影響。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設通過柵格的有效速度1.5 m/s、損失係數K=2，hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m；K已對應該速度定義，不再另加堵塞倍數。 堵塞不均會把水流集中到少數開口，引發局部振動與吸氣。差壓增加也可能來自流量增大，因此未正規化的趨勢不能直接當作堵塞程度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「攔污柵損失與堵塞」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Screens protect equipment but consume head, and blockage reduces open area. Loss coefficient and velocity must use compatible area definitions to avoid counting the blockage effect twice. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume effective screen velocity 1.5 m/s and loss coefficient K=2. hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m; K corresponds to that velocity definition, without another blockage multiplier. Uneven blockage concentrates flow through a few openings, promoting vibration and air entrainment. Increased differential head can also reflect increased flow, so an unnormalized trend does not directly measure blockage. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Screen losses and blockage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「差壓增加只可能來自攔污柵堵塞，與流量無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher screen differential head only indicates blockage and is unrelated to flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「攔污柵損失與堵塞」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Screen losses and blockage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-33-k1","title":"攔污柵損失與堵塞","titleEn":"Screen losses and blockage","text":"攔污柵保護設備卻增加水頭損失，堵塞使有效流通面積縮小。損失係數與速度必須使用相容的面積定義，否則會重複計算堵塞影響。","textEn":"Screens protect equipment but consume head, and blockage reduces open area. Loss coefficient and velocity must use compatible area definitions to avoid counting the blockage effect twice.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：差壓增加只可能來自攔污柵堵塞，與流量無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher screen differential head only indicates blockage and is unrelated to flow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「攔污柵損失與堵塞」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Screen losses and blockage\" is correct?","options":["攔污柵保護設備卻增加水頭損失，堵塞使有效流通面積縮小。","差壓增加只可能來自攔污柵堵塞，與流量無關。","罕見暴雨和罕見高潮可以不經檢查直接視為獨立。"],"optionsEn":["Screens protect equipment but consume head, and blockage reduces open area.","Higher screen differential head only indicates blockage and is unrelated to flow.","Rare rainfall and rare high tides can be assumed independent without checking."],"answer":0,"explanation":"攔污柵保護設備卻增加水頭損失，堵塞使有效流通面積縮小。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Screens protect equipment but consume head, and blockage reduces open area. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b225-v15-34","title":"攔污柵損失與堵塞：定量估算","titleEn":"Screen losses and blockage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「攔污柵損失與堵塞」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Screen losses and blockage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設通過柵格的有效速度1.5 m/s、損失係數K=2，hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m；K已對應該速度定義，不再另加堵塞倍數。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume effective screen velocity 1.5 m/s and loss coefficient K=2. hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m; K corresponds to that velocity definition, without another blockage multiplier. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步比較柵前後水位、流量與可見堵塞比例，建立清潔基線；檢查差壓管是否也被泥沙堵住，並將異常與雨後漂流物來源對照。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare upstream and downstream levels, flow and visible blockage against a clean baseline.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設通過柵格的有效速度1.5 m/s、損失係數K=2，hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m；K已對應該速度定義，不再另加堵塞倍數。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume effective screen velocity 1.5 m/s and loss coefficient K=2. hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m; K corresponds to that velocity definition, without another blockage multiplier.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「攔污柵損失與堵塞」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Screen losses and blockage\", which statement holds?","options":["水庫水位不變就表示沒有大量水量流入與流出。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","抽水機已經運轉就表示一定達到額定排水流量。"],"optionsEn":["An unchanged reservoir level means there is no substantial inflow or outflow.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","A running pump necessarily delivers its rated drainage flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b225-v15-35","title":"攔污柵損失與堵塞：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Screen losses and blockage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「攔污柵損失與堵塞」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Screen losses and blockage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步比較柵前後水位、流量與可見堵塞比例，建立清潔基線；檢查差壓管是否也被泥沙堵住，並將異常與雨後漂流物來源對照。將差壓除以速度平方建立清潔與堵塞曲線，確認量測差異不是單純流量增加。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare upstream and downstream levels, flow and visible blockage against a clean baseline. Check pressure connections for sediment blockage and relate anomalies to storm-driven debris sources. Normalize differential head by velocity squared and compare clean and blocked curves to exclude a simple increase in flow. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以攔污柵損失與堵塞編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。同步比較柵前後水位、流量與可見堵塞比例，建立清潔基線；檢查差壓管是否也被泥沙堵住，並將異常與雨後漂流物來源對照。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for screen losses and blockage, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare upstream and downstream levels, flow and visible blockage against a clean baseline. Check pressure connections for sediment blockage and relate anomalies to storm-driven debris sources.","failure":"注意干擾：堵塞不均會把水流集中到少數開口，引發局部振動與吸氣。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uneven blockage concentrates flow through a few openings, promoting vibration and air entrainment. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步比較柵前後水位、流量與可見堵塞比例，建立清潔基線；檢查差壓管是否也被泥沙堵住，並將異常與雨後漂流物來源對照。將差壓除以速度平方建立清潔與堵塞曲線，確認量測差異不是單純流量增加。","textEn":"Compare upstream and downstream levels, flow and visible blockage against a clean baseline. Check pressure connections for sediment blockage and relate anomalies to storm-driven debris sources. Normalize differential head by velocity squared and compare clean and blocked curves to exclude a simple increase in flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以攔污柵損失與堵塞編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。同步比較柵前後水位、流量與可見堵塞比例，建立清潔基線；檢查差壓管是否也被泥沙堵住，並將異常與雨後漂流物來源對照。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for screen losses and blockage, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare upstream and downstream levels, flow and visible blockage against a clean baseline. Check pressure connections for sediment blockage and relate anomalies to storm-driven debris sources.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「攔污柵損失與堵塞」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Screen losses and blockage\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","沒有明顯噪音就足以證明吸水條件有足夠餘裕。","同步比較柵前後水位、流量與可見堵塞比例，建立清潔基線；檢查差壓管是否也被泥沙堵住，並將異常與雨後漂流物來源對照。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Absence of obvious noise proves sufficient suction-head margin.","Compare upstream and downstream levels, flow and visible blockage against a clean baseline."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步比較柵前後水位、流量與可見堵塞比例，建立清潔基線；檢查差壓管是否也被泥沙堵住，並將異常與雨後漂流物來源對照。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare upstream and downstream levels, flow and visible blockage against a clean baseline. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b225-v15-36","title":"攔污柵損失與堵塞：失效診斷","titleEn":"Screen losses and blockage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「攔污柵損失與堵塞」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Screen losses and blockage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"堵塞不均會把水流集中到少數開口，引發局部振動與吸氣。差壓增加也可能來自流量增大，因此未正規化的趨勢不能直接當作堵塞程度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uneven blockage concentrates flow through a few openings, promoting vibration and air entrainment. Increased differential head can also reflect increased flow, so an unnormalized trend does not directly measure blockage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：差壓增加也可能來自流量增大，因此未正規化的趨勢不能直接當作堵塞程度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Increased differential head can also reflect increased flow, so an unnormalized trend does not directly measure blockage.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「差壓增加只可能來自攔污柵堵塞，與流量無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher screen differential head only indicates blockage and is unrelated to flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"堵塞不均會把水流集中到少數開口，引發局部振動與吸氣。差壓增加也可能來自流量增大，因此未正規化的趨勢不能直接當作堵塞程度。","textEn":"Uneven blockage concentrates flow through a few openings, promoting vibration and air entrainment. Increased differential head can also reflect increased flow, so an unnormalized trend does not directly measure blockage.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「攔污柵損失與堵塞」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Screen losses and blockage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["堵塞不均會把水流集中到少數開口，引發局部振動與吸氣。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","罕見暴雨和罕見高潮可以不經檢查直接視為獨立。"],"optionsEn":["Uneven blockage concentrates flow through a few openings, promoting vibration and air entrainment.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Rare rainfall and rare high tides can be assumed independent without checking."],"answer":0,"explanation":"堵塞不均會把水流集中到少數開口，引發局部振動與吸氣。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uneven blockage concentrates flow through a few openings, promoting vibration and air entrainment. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b225-v15-37","title":"複合事件與失效組合：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Compound events and failure combinations: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「複合事件與失效組合」如何影響新加坡濱海堤壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Compound events and failure combinations” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"暴雨、高海潮與電力限制可能同時發生，聯合機率取決於相關性。把各事件單獨罕見當成組合必定極罕見，會忽略共同氣象原因。 假設一年高海潮事件機率0.1，且該條件下強降雨機率0.3，聯合機率0.03；若誤用無條件雨率0.1獨立相乘會得到0.01。 樣本很少時條件機率不穩定，氣候變化又會改變共同分布。只列一個年機率而不說事件窗口，容易把短時設備容量與長期風險混為一談。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「複合事件與失效組合」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Heavy rain, high tide and power constraints can coincide, with joint probability depending on dependence. Individually rare events do not necessarily make their combination extremely rare when weather drives several conditions together. Assume annual high-tide event probability 0.1 and conditional heavy-rain probability 0.3. Joint probability is 0.03; incorrectly multiplying an unconditional rain probability 0.1 gives 0.01. Conditional probabilities are unstable with sparse samples, and climate changes alter joint distributions. Reporting one annual probability without its event window confuses short-term capacity with long-term risk. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Compound events and failure combinations” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設一年高海潮事件機率0.1，且該條件下強降雨機率0.3，聯合機率0.03；若誤用無條件雨率0.1獨立相乘會得到0.01。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume annual high-tide event probability 0.1 and conditional heavy-rain probability 0.3.","failure":"常見誤解：「罕見暴雨和罕見高潮可以不經檢查直接視為獨立。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Rare rainfall and rare high tides can be assumed independent without checking.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「複合事件與失效組合」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Compound events and failure combinations”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-37-k1","title":"複合事件與失效組合","titleEn":"Compound events and failure combinations","text":"暴雨、高海潮與電力限制可能同時發生，聯合機率取決於相關性。把各事件單獨罕見當成組合必定極罕見，會忽略共同氣象原因。","textEn":"Heavy rain, high tide and power constraints can coincide, with joint probability depending on dependence. Individually rare events do not necessarily make their combination extremely rare when weather drives several conditions together.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：罕見暴雨和罕見高潮可以不經檢查直接視為獨立。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Rare rainfall and rare high tides can be assumed independent without checking. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「複合事件與失效組合」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Compound events and failure combinations\" is correct?","options":["罕見暴雨和罕見高潮可以不經檢查直接視為獨立。","暴雨、高海潮與電力限制可能同時發生，聯合機率取決於相關性。","各分區最大流量無須考慮時序就能直接相加。"],"optionsEn":["Rare rainfall and rare high tides can be assumed independent without checking.","Heavy rain, high tide and power constraints can coincide, with joint probability depending on dependence.","Subcatchment peak discharges can be added directly without considering their timing."],"answer":1,"explanation":"暴雨、高海潮與電力限制可能同時發生，聯合機率取決於相關性。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Heavy rain, high tide and power constraints can coincide, with joint probability depending on dependence. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b225-v15-38","title":"複合事件與失效組合：定量估算","titleEn":"Compound events and failure combinations: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「複合事件與失效組合」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Compound events and failure combinations” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設一年高海潮事件機率0.1，且該條件下強降雨機率0.3，聯合機率0.03；若誤用無條件雨率0.1獨立相乘會得到0.01。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume annual high-tide event probability 0.1 and conditional heavy-rain probability 0.3. Joint probability is 0.03; incorrectly multiplying an unconditional rain probability 0.1 gives 0.01. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：明確定義事件窗口、雨量門檻與潮位基準，核對歷史事件是否同時而非僅同年；用情境矩陣連結庫容、泵可用度與供電狀態。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Define event window, rainfall threshold and tidal datum, checking coincidence rather than merely the same calendar year.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設一年高海潮事件機率0.1，且該條件下強降雨機率0.3，聯合機率0.03；若誤用無條件雨率0.1獨立相乘會得到0.01。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume annual high-tide event probability 0.1 and conditional heavy-rain probability 0.3. Joint probability is 0.03; incorrectly multiplying an unconditional rain probability 0.1 gives 0.01.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「複合事件與失效組合」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Compound events and failure combinations\", which statement holds?","options":["平均庫位高於海面就保證所有瞬間都向海排水。","並聯兩台相同泵的總流量必定是單台的兩倍。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設一年高海潮事件機率0.1，且該條件下強降雨機率0.3，聯合機率0.03；若誤用無條件雨率0.1獨立相乘會得到0.01。"],"optionsEn":["A higher mean reservoir level guarantees outward flow at every instant.","Two identical parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume annual high-tide event probability 0.1 and conditional heavy-rain probability 0.3."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設一年高海潮事件機率0.1，且該條件下強降雨機率0.3，聯合機率0.03；若誤用無條件雨率0.1獨立相乘會得到0.01。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume annual high-tide event probability 0.1 and conditional heavy-rain probability 0.3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b225-v15-39","title":"複合事件與失效組合：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Compound events and failure combinations: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「複合事件與失效組合」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Compound events and failure combinations” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"明確定義事件窗口、雨量門檻與潮位基準，核對歷史事件是否同時而非僅同年；用情境矩陣連結庫容、泵可用度與供電狀態。用相同事件時間窗口重算條件機率，並報告小樣本區間及相關性假設的敏感度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Define event window, rainfall threshold and tidal datum, checking coincidence rather than merely the same calendar year. Link storage, pump availability and power condition in a scenario matrix. Recalculate conditional probabilities with a consistent event window and report small-sample ranges and sensitivity to dependence assumptions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以複合事件與失效組合編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。明確定義事件窗口、雨量門檻與潮位基準，核對歷史事件是否同時而非僅同年；用情境矩陣連結庫容、泵可用度與供電狀態。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for compound events and failure combinations, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Define event window, rainfall threshold and tidal datum, checking coincidence rather than merely the same calendar year. Link storage, pump availability and power condition in a scenario matrix.","failure":"注意干擾：樣本很少時條件機率不穩定，氣候變化又會改變共同分布。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Conditional probabilities are unstable with sparse samples, and climate changes alter joint distributions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"明確定義事件窗口、雨量門檻與潮位基準，核對歷史事件是否同時而非僅同年；用情境矩陣連結庫容、泵可用度與供電狀態。用相同事件時間窗口重算條件機率，並報告小樣本區間及相關性假設的敏感度。","textEn":"Define event window, rainfall threshold and tidal datum, checking coincidence rather than merely the same calendar year. Link storage, pump availability and power condition in a scenario matrix. Recalculate conditional probabilities with a consistent event window and report small-sample ranges and sensitivity to dependence assumptions.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以複合事件與失效組合編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。明確定義事件窗口、雨量門檻與潮位基準，核對歷史事件是否同時而非僅同年；用情境矩陣連結庫容、泵可用度與供電狀態。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for compound events and failure combinations, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Define event window, rainfall threshold and tidal datum, checking coincidence rather than merely the same calendar year. Link storage, pump availability and power condition in a scenario matrix.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「複合事件與失效組合」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Compound events and failure combinations\"?","options":["明確定義事件窗口、雨量門檻與潮位基準，核對歷史事件是否同時而非僅同年；用情境矩陣連結庫容、泵可用度與供電狀態。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","平均鹽度很低就表示所有深度的水質完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Define event window, rainfall threshold and tidal datum, checking coincidence rather than merely the same calendar year.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Low mean salinity means water quality is identical at every depth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"明確定義事件窗口、雨量門檻與潮位基準，核對歷史事件是否同時而非僅同年；用情境矩陣連結庫容、泵可用度與供電狀態。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Define event window, rainfall threshold and tidal datum, checking coincidence rather than merely the same calendar year. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b225-v15-40","title":"複合事件與失效組合：失效診斷","titleEn":"Compound events and failure combinations: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b225-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「複合事件與失效組合」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Compound events and failure combinations” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"樣本很少時條件機率不穩定，氣候變化又會改變共同分布。只列一個年機率而不說事件窗口，容易把短時設備容量與長期風險混為一談。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Conditional probabilities are unstable with sparse samples, and climate changes alter joint distributions. Reporting one annual probability without its event window confuses short-term capacity with long-term risk. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只列一個年機率而不說事件窗口，容易把短時設備容量與長期風險混為一談。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Reporting one annual probability without its event window confuses short-term capacity with long-term risk.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「罕見暴雨和罕見高潮可以不經檢查直接視為獨立。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Rare rainfall and rare high tides can be assumed independent without checking.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b225-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"樣本很少時條件機率不穩定，氣候變化又會改變共同分布。只列一個年機率而不說事件窗口，容易把短時設備容量與長期風險混為一談。","textEn":"Conditional probabilities are unstable with sparse samples, and climate changes alter joint distributions. Reporting one annual probability without its event window confuses short-term capacity with long-term risk.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b225-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「複合事件與失效組合」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Compound events and failure combinations\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","樣本很少時條件機率不穩定，氣候變化又會改變共同分布。","各分區最大流量無須考慮時序就能直接相加。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Conditional probabilities are unstable with sparse samples, and climate changes alter joint distributions.","Subcatchment peak discharges can be added directly without considering their timing."],"answer":1,"explanation":"樣本很少時條件機率不穩定，氣候變化又會改變共同分布。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Conditional probabilities are unstable with sparse samples, and climate changes alter joint distributions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-pub-marina","v15s-pub-marina-faq","v15s-pub-marina-book","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
